<section id="when-ukca" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">8. When UKCA Still Makes Sense</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">UKCA isn't mandatory for most chargers in GB, but it can still be useful.</p>
 <ul class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
 <li><strong>Retailer or marketplace requirements.</strong> Some buyers ask for UKCA documentation even when CE is accepted. If a retailer requires it, dual marking may be the simplest commercial answer.</li>
 <li><strong>Future divergence.</strong> If the UK changes a designated standard or introduces a new requirement, a UKCA file may be easier to update than a CE-only file.</li>
 <li><strong>Packaging already retooled.</strong> If the packaging already carries UKCA, keeping it is low-risk where the conditions are met.</li>
 <li><strong>Dual-market labeling.</strong> Some brands prefer one label for GB and NI. Remember that UKCA alone isn't valid in NI, and CE plus UKNI has its own conditions.</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">UKCA isn't a substitute for CE in Northern Ireland or the EU. It's also not a substitute for the UK importer file. The mark is only one part of the compliance package.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

<section id="verify-supplier" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-xl p-6 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-6">9. How to Verify a Supplier's UK Compliance File</h2>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">A supplier's claim is only as good as the documents behind it. Verify the file, not the logo on the quotation.</p>

 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">Check the UK DoC</h3>
 <ol class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-decimal pl-5">
 <li>Does it reference the UK statutory instrument, not only the EU directive?</li>
 <li>Does it list the GB designated standards used?</li>
 <li>Does it identify the exact model and plug variant?</li>
 <li>Is it signed and dated by the manufacturer or authorised representative?</li>
 </ol>

 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">Check the technical file</h3>
 <ol class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-decimal pl-5">
 <li>Do the test reports match the model you're buying?</li>
 <li>Do they cover the radio configuration if the charger has Bluetooth or Wi-Fi?</li>
 <li>Is the file complete enough to support the UK DoC?</li>
 <li>Can the factory explain which regulations apply?</li>
 </ol>

 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto mb-8">
 <img src="/image/blog/gan-charger/gan-charger-testing-data.webp"
 srcset="/image/blog/gan-charger/gan-charger-testing-data-900w.webp 900w, /image/blog/gan-charger/gan-charger-testing-data.webp 1706w"
 sizes="(min-width: 1440px) 798px, (min-width: 1280px) 798px, (min-width: 1024px) 798px, (min-width: 768px) 670px, (min-width: 430px) 332px, 277px"
