 width="1706" height="1279" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
 class="rounded-2xl shadow-lg w-full">
 </div>

 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">Check the plug and fuse</h3>
 <ol class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-decimal pl-5">
 <li>Is the plug a BS 1363 standard plug?</li>
 <li>Is the fuse a BS 1362 fuse with the correct rating?</li>
 <li>If a conversion plug is used, is it notified-body approved and tool-removable?</li>
 <li>Does the packaging match the plug variant?</li>
 </ol>

 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">Check the importer and EPR details</h3>
 <ol class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-decimal pl-5">
 <li>Is the importer's name and address on the product or permitted packaging?</li>
 <li>Has the importer registered for WEEE and batteries where required?</li>
 <li>Does the label show the crossed-out wheeled bin and date mark where applicable?</li>
 </ol>

 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue uppercase mb-3">Red flags</h3>
 <ul class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4 space-y-2 list-disc pl-5">
 <li>"UKCA is mandatory, CE is dead" with no reference to the 2024 amendment.</li>
 <li>A CE DoC with the EU directive name and no UK statutory instrument.</li>
 <li>A UKCA mark on the box but no UK DoC.</li>
 <li>An EU plug with a travel adaptor in the box.</li>
 <li>A test report for a similar model, not the model you're buying.</li>
 <li>No importer name or address on the product or packaging.</li>
 <li>A supplier who can't explain the difference between GB and NI.</li>
 </ul>
 <p class="text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">For a step-by-step certificate check, see our <a href="/blog/verify-fake-charger-certificates-fcc-ce-ul/" class="text-brandOrange hover:underline">guide to verifying FCC and CE charger certificates</a>.</p>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

