<!-- 9. FAQ -->
<!-- ============================================================ -->
<section id="faq" class="mb-16">
 <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6">
 <div class="bg-slate-50 rounded-2xl p-8 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm">
 <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-brandBlue uppercase italic mb-8 text-center">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>

 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm mb-6 text-center max-w-3xl mx-auto">The most common questions from UK charger importers about CE, UKCA, and the importer file, answered with the regulation and the practical checks that apply:</p>

 <div class="space-y-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto">

 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Is UKCA mandatory for chargers in Great Britain in 2026?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">No. CE is recognised indefinitely in GB for the 21 regulations covered by the 2024 amendment, and UKCA is voluntary for most chargers. Some sectors have separate rules, so confirm the product category.</p>
 </div>

 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Is CE still valid in the UK?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">Yes, in Great Britain. In Northern Ireland, CE is the required mark, and CE plus UKNI applies when a UK body carried out mandatory third-party assessment. UKCA alone is not accepted in Northern Ireland.</p>
 </div>

 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">What is the 31 December 2027 deadline?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">It is the end of the labelling easement for UKCA and importer information. It is not a CE expiry date, and it does not make UKCA mandatory on 1 January 2028.</p>
 </div>

 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Does a charger need a BS 1363 plug?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">For appliances intended for domestic use at 200V or above, yes. The charger needs a BS 1363 plug with a BS 1362 fuse, or a notified-body-approved conversion plug that requires a tool to remove. A travel adaptor does not count.</p>
 </div>

 <div class="bg-white rounded-xl p-6 faq-answer">
 <h3 class="font-black text-brandBlue mb-2">Do I need UK WEEE or battery producer registration?</h3>
 <p class="text-slate-600 text-sm">If you import EEE commercially into the UK, you are likely an EEE producer. If you are first in the selling chain to make batteries available on the UK market, you are likely a battery producer. Thresholds and deadlines apply, and battery weight is reported separately.</p>
 </div>

 </div>
 </div>
 </div>
</section>

